<title>GERMANY: Thyssen, Krupp suspended all day.</title>
<headline>Thyssen, Krupp suspended all day.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Thyssen AG and Fried. Krupp AG Hoesch-Krupp will remain suspended for the whole of Wednesday pending further announcements relating to Krupp's takeover bid for Thyssen, a spokesman for the Frankfurt stock exchange said.</p>
<p>The bourse had said on Tuesday evening the shares would resume trade as normal on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended on Tuesday ahead of Krupp's announcement that it was bidding 435 marks ($260) per Thyssen share in a rare 13.6 billion-mark hostile takeover bid.</p>
<p>The offer sparked an angry response from Thyssen, which recommended that shareholders do nothing while it prepared its response to the unwelcome bid.</p>
<p>Thyssen shares closed floor trade at 346.80 marks on Monday. Krupp closed at 272 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.674 German Marks)</p>
